An AI Ecosystem Breeder is not a gardener, not a farmer, not a lab technician. They are the evolutionary conductor of a living, breathing, sealed world. While the Artificial Biosphere Architect designs the physical and chemical architecture of the life-support system, the AI Ecosystem Breeder ensures the biological components inside it — microbes, plants, insects, fungi — do not drift into dysfunction over time. They wield AI not as a monitoring tool but as a co-evolutionary engine, accelerating adaptation, suppressing pathological shifts, and guiding the biosphere toward long-term stability.

This profession exists because a sealed ecosystem has no wilderness. It has no vast atmospheric buffer, no migratory escape routes, no redundant trophic webs spanning continents. Every microbial bloom, every nutrient imbalance, every unexpected genetic drift is a potential cascade failure. The breeder's job is to stay ahead of evolution itself.

