Key conclusion: Escape rate is a function of the environment, not the genetic circuit alone. A strain validated in hydroponic solution (low nutrient, pH 6.0) will have a different escape rate when it enters a soil‑analog module rich in organic acids.

D.2 Combinatorial Containment — Safety Margin Calculation

If a strain carries two independent containment mechanisms (A and B) with per‑generation escape rates p_A and p_B (measured in the target module), the joint escape probability per generation, assuming independence, is:

p_{\text{combined}} = p_A \times p_B

For example, with auxotrophy (p_A = 10^{-7}) and an inducible kill switch (p_B = 10^{-6}), the theoretical combined escape rate is 10^{-13}. Over 10^{10} cells (a typical small bloom), the expected number of escape mutants is 10^{-3}, i.e., essentially zero. Adding a third mechanism (genetic entanglement of essential genes) reduces this further.

Independence verification: Before release, the breeder must experimentally demonstrate that the two mechanisms do not share a common escape pathway (e.g., a single mutation that simultaneously inactivates both). This is done by passaging the dual‑containment strain in the target module medium for 100 generations and deep‑sequencing any survivors to identify the causative mutations. Only when no single‑mutation double‑escape events are observed can independence be assumed.

D.3 Per‑Module Validation Protocol (derived from [14] and [15])

1. Sample the module’s primary aqueous medium (hydroponic solution, soil pore water, condensate) and full‑chemical‑analysis.
2. Inoculate the contained strain into 100 mL of that medium at 10^7 CFU/mL, in triplicate.
3. Incubate under module‑representative conditions (temperature, light, dissolved O₂/CO₂).
4. Passage daily for 30 days (approx. 120–200 generations, depending on growth rate).
5. Screen for escape mutants each day by plating on selective medium (e.g., medium lacking the auxotrophic supplement, or at non‑permissive temperature).
6. Compute escape rate via fluctuation analysis (MSS‑maximum likelihood method).
7. Qualify the strain for that module only if the 95% upper confidence bound on escape rate is <10^{-8} per generation for each individual mechanism and <10^{-14} for the combined stack.

This protocol is formalised as Lunar Biocontainment Standard Operating Procedure LUN‑BC‑2039.01, required before any release under the Containment Honesty Principle (Section 9.5).

